# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependency staging plan for the 950PR x86_64 image.
#
# Every artefact that deps/950pr-x86_64/ must contain for
# Dockerfile.x86_64 to build with --network=none. targets/target-950pr/build.sh reads
# this file and refuses to start until each row is satisfied, so the plan is
# enforced rather than merely written down.
#
# Format:  kind | path relative to DEPS_DIR | bytes | sha256 | source
#   kind    file | dir | glob
#   bytes   0 means "not size-checked" (directories, and sets whose size
#           depends on the resolve)
#   sha256  '-' means UNPINNED. Sizes were measured with HTTP range requests
#           against the live bucket on 2026-09-05. The two CANN hashes below
#           are no longer '-': they are pinned from the first fully verified
#           fetch (2026-09-05, both files downloaded to their exact expected
#           byte count), the way download_deps.sh already does for the 8.5.0
#           artefacts. The wheelhouse and apt rows stay unpinned because their
#           contents depend on the resolve.
#
# CANN 9.1.0 IS THE PINNED LINE, and it is real: probing the Huawei OBS bucket
# the way download_deps.sh documents returns 206 for 9.0.0 and 9.1.0 and 403
# ("no such version string") for 8.6.x, 9.0.RC1, 9.1.RC1, 9.2.0 and 9.5.0.
# quay.io/ascend/cann publishes matching 9.1.0-950-* images, and upstream
# vllm-ascend's Dockerfile.a5 builds on 9.1.0-950-ubuntu22.04-py3.12.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- CANN 9.1.0, x86_64 ----------------------------------------------------
file|Ascend-cann-toolkit_9.1.0_linux-x86_64.run|1298337341|69e52e49a5ac1dde756a0d72077e36df7382b37cd3e1d78005d9cdbf699aeafc|https://ascend-repo.obs.cn-east-2.myhuaweicloud.com/CANN/CANN%209.1.0/Ascend-cann-toolkit_9.1.0_linux-x86_64.run
file|Ascend-cann-nnal_9.1.0_linux-x86_64.run|572750476|1a743a0957a77a0624c2ecfdf689b5c5937a9097fda1e3b3e8e0191a7d11c694|https://ascend-repo.obs.cn-east-2.myhuaweicloud.com/CANN/CANN%209.1.0/Ascend-cann-nnal_9.1.0_linux-x86_64.run

# --- CANN runtime libraries the standalone toolkit omits -------------------
# The public 9.1.0 toolkit is an incomplete slice of a CANN install: its lib64
# holds 150 shared objects against the 176 in Huawei's own image for this SoC.
# Three of the missing twenty-six are load-bearing - libopapi.so (vllm-ascend
# links -lopapi for every SoC), libopapi_math.so (the compiled custom-ops
# package will not install without it) and libhccl.so (torch_npu's DT_NEEDED).
# No published .run carries them: kernels-{950,a5,910b} and nnrt all return 403.
# They are lifted out of the vendor image's layer blob instead - the same route
# the 310P used for libhccl.so on CANN 8.5.0.
dir|cann_extra/lib64|0|-|quay.io/ascend/cann:9.1.0-950-ubuntu22.04-py3.10 layer blob
file|cann_extra/lib64/libopapi.so|0|-|same layer
file|cann_extra/lib64/libopapi_math.so|0|-|same layer
file|cann_extra/lib64/libhccl.so|0|-|same layer

# --- vllm-ascend ACLNN third-party archives --------------------------------
# csrc/build_aclnn.sh builds 27 custom ops on the ascend950 branch and its
# CMake FetchContent-downloads these from gitcode.com unless they are already
# under ${CANN_3RD_LIB_PATH} (which defaults to csrc/third_party). makeself is
# NOT staged here - CANN ships its own copy and the Dockerfile copies that in.
dir|third_party/pkg|0|-|https://gitcode.com/cann-src-third-party
file|third_party/pkg/abseil-cpp-20230802.1.tar.gz|0|-|abseil-cpp/releases/download/20230802.1
file|third_party/pkg/protobuf-25.1.tar.gz|0|-|protobuf/releases/download/v25.1
file|third_party/json/include/nlohmann/json.hpp|0|-|json/releases/download/v3.11.3/include.zip

# --- Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy, amd64) local apt archive -------------------------
# The .deb closure of targets/target-950pr/packages/sys_packages.txt plus a
# dpkg-scanpackages index, built the way common/scripts/fetch_debs.sh does for the
# 310P but in a jammy container and with no QEMU in the way. Jammy because
# that is the base upstream's Dockerfile.a5 builds on; clang-15 resolves out
# of jammy-updates, which the stock ubuntu:22.04 image has enabled.
dir|apt_debs|0|-|apt-get install --download-only inside ubuntu:22.04
file|apt_debs/Packages.gz|0|-|dpkg-scanpackages . > Packages && gzip -k Packages

# --- cp310 / manylinux x86_64 wheelhouse -----------------------------------
# Resolved from targets/target-950pr/requirements/python_wheels.txt. cp310, not
# cp312, because the base is now Ubuntu 22.04 and jammy's system interpreter is
# python3.10; every pin in that file publishes a cp310 manylinux_2_28 x86_64
# wheel, and jammy's glibc 2.35 clears that floor.
#
# torch-npu 2.10.0.post4 is on PyPI: 2.10.0/.post2/.post4/.post6 ship as
# cp310-cp313 manylinux_2_28 wheels for x86_64 and aarch64. triton-ascend 3.2.2
# is the mirror-only one (PyPI stops at 3.2.0), and its index sits at the ROOT
# of the mirror path - a /simple/ prefix returns 404. Most likely staging
# failure; see docs/target-950pr-x86_64.md.
dir|python_wheels|0|-|pip download -r requirements/python_wheels.txt
glob|python_wheels/torch-2.10.0*.whl|0|-|https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
glob|python_wheels/torch_npu-2.10.0.post4*.whl|0|-|https://pypi.org/simple
glob|python_wheels/triton_ascend-3.2.2*.whl|0|-|https://mirrors.huaweicloud.com/ascend/repos/pypi

# The vLLM wheel is BUILT, not downloaded: PyPI's x86_64 vllm is a CUDA build.
# Build v0.27.1 from source with VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=empty and drop the wheel
# here, exactly as the 310P pipeline does via common/scripts/build_vllm_wheel.sh.
glob|python_wheels/vllm-0.27.1*.whl|0|-|built from source, VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=empty

# --- vllm-ascend source ----------------------------------------------------
# Built from source in stage 6. No patches are applied for this target.
# Staged from the codeload tarball rather than a git clone: the Dockerfile
# deletes .git anyway (setuptools-scm is fed VLLM_ASCEND_VERSION), and a
# depth-1 clone over the git protocol cannot resume a dropped connection.
file|src/vllm-ascend/setup.py|0|-|https://codeload.github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/tar.gz/refs/heads/main
file|src/vllm-ascend/requirements.txt|0|-|same checkout

# The catlass submodule, which a tarball does NOT carry - it ships the empty
# directory only. csrc/build_aclnn.sh takes the ascend950 branch, calls
# setup_catlass_dependency(), and runs `git submodule update` when
# csrc/third_party/catlass/include is absent; with --network=none that fails
# and takes the vllm-ascend wheel build with it. Staging include/ is enough,
# because the script skips the fetch when it is already there. The commit is
# pinned by vllm-ascend's own .gitmodules, not chosen here.
dir|src/vllm-ascend/csrc/third_party/catlass/include|0|-|https://gitcode.com/cann/catlass.git @ .gitmodules commit
